<h2>The San Marcos River and flood risk in Martindale</h2>
<p>The San Marcos River runs downstream from San Marcos toward Martindale, so heavy rain upstream can affect properties here even when local rainfall is modest. During the Halloween flood of October 31, 2013, the National Weather Service documented <a href="https://www.weather.gov/media/ewx/wxevents/ewx-20131031.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the San Marcos River flooding over FM 1979 near Martindale</a>. Upstream, rainfall that night reached 6 to 10 inches across much of Hays County and 12 to 14 inches from Wimberley to Driftwood.</p>
<p>On May 24, 2015, the <a href="https://www.weather.gov/media/ewx/wxevents/ewx-20150524.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">San Marcos River near San Marcos crested at 43.08 feet</a> after the Blanco River flood. Those Hays County readings are not Martindale measurements, but they show how much water the river system can carry toward Caldwell County.</p>
<h3>What this means for your insurance</h3>
