<h2>Storms and freezes in Caldwell County</h2>
<p>Martindale sees the same spring hail, damaging thunderstorm winds, and occasional hard freezes as the rest of the I-35 region. During Winter Storm Uri on February 15, 2021, NWS spotters in Caldwell County reported <a href="https://www.weather.gov/media/ewx/wxevents/ewx-20210218.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roughly 3.3 to 4.8 inches of snow</a>, followed by days of extreme cold that burst pipes across Central Texas.</p>
<p>The storm statistics on our <a href="/storm-history/">storm history page</a> come from NOAA records for Hays County, which begins just west of Martindale. Our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a> can show Hays County reports within your chosen radius of Martindale. For events recorded inside Caldwell County, search the <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA Storm Events Database</a>.</p>

<h2>Common claims for Martindale properties</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Roof damage from hail and wind.</strong> Shingle and metal roofs on homes, barns, and sheds. See <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof damage claims</a> and <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Fallen trees.</strong> Large trees near the river and along property lines can come down on roofs and fences in high winds. See <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">wind damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Freeze damage.</strong> Exposed plumbing, well equipment, and water heaters are vulnerable in hard freezes. See <a href="/services/freeze-damage-claims/">freeze damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Water damage.</strong> Plumbing failures and storm-created leaks inside the home. See <a href="/services/water-damage-claims/">water damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Small business losses.</strong> Building, inventory, and income questions under a commercial policy. See <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claims</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Permits in Martindale</h2>
<p>Martindale is an incorporated city, so ask the City of Martindale what it requires before roof replacement, structural work, or rebuilding after water damage. Properties outside city limits in unincorporated Caldwell County follow county requirements, including any floodplain rules. Insurers pay code-required upgrades only to the extent your policy’s ordinance or law coverage allows. Our <a href="/local-building-codes/">building codes guide</a> explains the general rules.</p>

<h2>How a San Marcos public adjuster helps in Martindale</h2>
<p>We represent policyholders only. For a Martindale claim, we inspect the home and other structures, separate damage by cause so the right policy responds, review your coverage, prepare a detailed estimate, and handle communication with the insurer. If your claim was <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied</a> or <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid</a>, we can review the file with you. We cannot promise a particular result; coverage depends on your policy and the facts.</p>
